WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.600
An Israeli

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.601
American citizen

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.203
was killed today in the West Bank.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.771
This follows an eruption of violence

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.739
over the weekend

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:07.240
when rare peace talks between Israeli

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.875
and Palestinian officials in Jordan

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:09.909
were overshadowed

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.644
by attacks and riots back

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.446
home, sparked by the shooting

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:13.913
of two

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.182
Israeli brothers near a Palestinian town.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.251
Israeli officials quickly dubbed that

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.419
a terrorist attack

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:21.721
and hours later, riots broke out

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.390
almost a pogrom, really.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.758
Israeli settlers

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:25.658
throwing rocks

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.093
and setting houses and Palestinian

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.728
neighborhoods ablaze.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.296
It was shocking and horrifying.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:30.864
At least one

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.599
Palestinian was shot and killed.

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.266
CNN's

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.801
Hadas Gold is in Jerusalem

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.903
with more on what Israeli officials call

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.806
revenge attacks.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.876
Benjamin Netanyahu

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.277
is the most experienced

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.413
prime minister in Israeli history,

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.213
but he's facing

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.849
unprecedented, multifaceted battles

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.751
on nearly every front

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:52.952
between the

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:53.887
tensions and violence

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:54.621
between Israelis

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.923
and Palestinians at a 20 year high.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:57.991
On Sunday,

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:58.792
the occupied West

00:00:58.792 --> 00:00:59.592
Bank burned

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.694
two Israeli brothers shot point-Blank

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.463
killed while sitting in traffic

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.464
in what officials say was

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:07.534
a terrorist attack, which was then

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.368
in what's been deemed

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.537
revenge attacks by Israeli settlers.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.605
A Palestinian man shot and killed

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.874
houses and cars burned

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.309
just hours after Israeli

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.811
and Palestinian officials

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:19.345
met in a summit in Jordan meant

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.413
to calm tensions.

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:22.782
A joint communique pledging

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.150
to take steps to restore

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.719
calm, seeking a just and lasting peace.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.856
So the Knesset gave

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:31.524
Meanwhile, Netanyahu's far right

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.792
wing coalition partners

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.094
seemingly dismissing

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.628
the summit in Jordan.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.763
The messages coming out.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.665
Netanyahu biographer Anshel Pfeffer

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.333
says much of the controversy around

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.401
Netanyahu is

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.770
thanks to these governing partners.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.872
I think this is the least

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.474
Netanyahu has ever been in control

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:48.775
as a prime minister.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.376
He's not basically he's

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.744
not running his government.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.279
His government is being run

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.647
by the coalition partners

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.850
who have him over a barrel.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.153
Meanwhile, for eight weeks in a row,

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.688
tens of thousands of Israelis

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.056
have been taking to the streets

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:03.957
to protest

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.525
against Netanyahu's planned

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:08.027
massive judicial reforms.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.662
The most sweeping of these changes

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.964
would give the Israeli parliament

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.432
the power to overturn

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.100
Supreme Court decisions.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.168
Many critics are arguing it's

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:15.969
part of a ploy

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:16.903
to help Netanyahu

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.705
out of his ongoing corruption trial.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.473
Something he denies.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.941
Good to see you, Sir Thomas.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:22.509
Good to see you.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.409
Netanyahu faces

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.044
increasing international pressure

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.313
from allies, notably the United States,

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.214
which has criticized

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.816
not only settlement expansion

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.217
and some of Israel's actions

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.785
in the occupied West Bank,

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.155
but also a rare presidential incursion

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.323
into internal Israeli politics.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.158
President Biden

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.659
urging a consensus be reached

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.561
on the judicial reforms.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:42.929
We've never had

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.230
this kind of differences

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.832
between Jerusalem and Washington.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:46.466
It's always been over

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.400
the Palestinian issue.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.968
It's been over the Iran issue.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.803
It's never been about the way

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.772
the Israeli government is

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.441
is legislating on a democratic agenda.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:56.075
We

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:58.912
looming ahead in the calendar

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.413
the highly sensitive period

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.681
of overlapping Muslim

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.081
and Jewish

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.350
holidays of Ramadan and Passover,

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:05.351
threatening to set

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:08.955
Jerusalem aflame as well

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.024
Yet another battlefront

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.358
for Netanyahu, Israel's

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.493
ultimate survivor.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:16.796
For now, Ben

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.898
and Jake, what's really interesting about

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.066
those settler rampages

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.034
is that the Israeli

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.203
military is actually calling them

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.771
acts of terror,

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.372
sort of rare moment agreement

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.774
with Palestinian officials.

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:28.575
We know that at least eight

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:30.410
people have been arrested

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.744
in connection to those attacks.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.313
Meanwhile, the Israeli military

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:34.847
sending extra battalions

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:35.715
into the West Bank

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.750
to try and catch the attackers

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.252
in those two attacks on the Israelis,

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.420
as well, as they say,

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.588
try to at least

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:42.689
keep the two sides

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:44.624
separated between Israeli

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.025
settlers and Palestinians.

